340
00:16:30,905 --&gt; 00:16:33,935
I just think people are still upset
that I went to the Warriors, and a

00:16:33.575 --> 00:16:38.163
lotta people who are Cavs fans who
enjoy watching the Cavs beat y'all

00:16:38.205 --> 00:16:40.958
before, um, which is a lot of people.
- Mmhmm.

00:16:41.125 --> 00:16:45.504
- I didn't realize that till I got, a lotta
people enjoyed seeing y'all lose in 2016.

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:49.258
And a lotta those people were
upset that we were so good.

00:16:49.508 --> 00:16:52.845
And they're still upset. Because
you do the same shit on Twitter.
- Mmhmm.

00:16:53.470 --> 00:16:55.347
- Damian Lillard does the
same shit on Twitter.
- Mmhmm.

00:16:55.597 --> 00:16:57.558
- CJ McCollum does the same shit on Twitter.

00:16:57.933 --> 00:17:00.769
We all do the same shit on
Twitter, but for me it's a problem.

00:17:00.894 --> 00:17:04.857
I mean, I chalk it up to just me being
so good at what I do and playing

00:17:04.857 --> 00:17:06.442
with a team that was so great.

00:17:06.942 --> 00:17:08.277
And we fit so well.

00:17:08.402 --> 00:17:09.653
Nobody likes a great thing.
- Mmhmm.

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:12.114
- And I was, I guess I was the cause of that

00:17:12.948 --> 00:17:14.700
great thing because I came and joined.

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:17.077
So it's way deeper than
what I do on Twitter.

00:17:17.578 --> 00:17:18.537
And I understand that.

00:17:18.537 --> 00:17:22.207
And it's funny to me at this point
because you can't erase what we did.

00:17:22.207 --> 00:17:23.333
You never gonna erase it.

00:17:23.417 --> 00:17:25.210
And you know you loved watchin' us play.

00:17:25.836 --> 00:17:27.337
You know what I'm saying?
- Facts, though, man.

00:17:27.337 --> 00:17:29.882
I think it's the best era of
basketball ever, in my opinion.

00:17:30.132 --> 00:17:31.216
But that's really what it is.

00:17:31.258 --> 00:17:34.678
So many people still upset with me
that I chose to play basketball for

00:17:34.678 --> 00:17:38.640
the Golden State Warriors, which is sad
at this point, cuz it's almost a

00:17:38.891 --> 00:17:41.935
decade later
- Mmhmm.
- since I made that decision,

00:17:41.935 --> 00:17:42.603
you know what I'm saying?

00:17:42.686 --> 00:17:46.065
Cuz that's never going to stop me
from engaging with fans cuz at the

00:17:46.065 --> 00:17:49.943
end of the day, I'm only talking about
basketball.
- Mmhmm.
- I'm not diving into politics.

00:17:49.943 --> 00:17:51.487
I'm not telling you how you should live.

00:17:51.779 --> 00:17:54.490
I'm not flexing my money or
my power or none of that.

00:17:55.991 --> 00:17:59.578
I'm just literally talking about the game,
- Mmhmm.
- you know, and what I see, and I

00:17:59.578 --> 00:18:00.704
don't think it harms anyone.

00:18:01.163 --> 00:18:05.542
- I would love to see D-Book win a
championship, but in my opinion, the

00:18:05.542 --> 00:18:14.218
Finals does not compare to Warriors-Cavs,
Warriors…
- Nah, mm-mm.
- Even, even Warriors-Raptors.

00:18:14.301 --> 00:18:16.637
Do you have any regrets about that

00:18:16.637 --> 00:18:19.723
knowing that we probably woulda
won five more championships?

00:18:20.182 --> 00:18:22.309
- Nah, I don't have
any regrets at all.

00:18:22.309 --> 00:18:24.228
I felt like we did exactly
what we were supposed to do.

00:18:25.020 --> 00:18:27.481
And I wish we woulda three-peated
because that's rare.

00:18:27.981 --> 00:18:29.274
And we were, like, right there.

00:18:30.109 --> 00:18:33.654
Um, but I don't have any regrets at
all cuz I felt like if we'd

00:18:33.654 --> 00:18:36.824
stayed healthy with the Nets, we had
a great chance of finishing too.
- Mmhmm.

00:18:37.199 --> 00:18:43.330
- So, um, nah, I mean, being hurt for that
year really changed my perspective on

00:18:43.330 --> 00:18:47.626
everything I was doing and everything
I did before. I looked at that time with

00:18:47.626 --> 00:18:51.421
playing with the Warriors as so special
to me, but it was time to move on.

00:18:52.548 --> 00:18:57.928
- So now you're in this
space with the Nets, and, you know,

00:18:57.928 --> 00:19:03.183
everybody has made this big deal
about Kyrie and, you know, his beliefs

00:19:03.225 --> 00:19:07.896
and out here missing games, and just
like we all do, he got his shit.

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:08.272
- Yeah.

00:19:08.438 --> 00:19:12.943
- And a lotta people are now
saying that this was going to cost

00:19:13.026 --> 00:19:17.614
y'all ultimately of reaching where
y'all wanna reach. What do you

00:19:17.614 --> 00:19:21.201
make of that?
-  I mean, I just think people don't like Kyrie because he

00:19:21.827 --> 00:19:23.954
wanted to leave Cleveland
and he wanted to leave Boston.

00:19:24.496 --> 00:19:25.831
I don't think it's any deeper than that.

00:19:26.498 --> 00:19:27.583
He doesn't harm anyone.

00:19:27.583 --> 00:19:30.335
He hasn't said anything that's
disrespectful to anybody.

00:19:31.128 --> 00:19:33.088
His game is beautiful to watch.

00:19:33.213 --> 00:19:36.508
I just think people don't like the
decisions on where he chooses to play.

00:19:37.259 --> 00:19:39.595
Um, and they sorta
amplify everything.

00:19:39.595 --> 00:19:41.513
Cuz everybody in this
league has their shit.
- Mmhmm.

00:19:41.638 --> 00:19:45.017
- They may say something over
a course of six months that

00:19:45.017 --> 00:19:46.185
may, everybody may not agree with.

00:19:46.643 --> 00:19:48.604
That's just the nature of our business.

00:19:48.854 --> 00:19:52.232
You know, when you're that good at
what you do, everything is a little

00:19:52.232 --> 00:19:56.195
amplified, and sometimes it's a little
extra, you know. So what Kyrie does,

00:19:56.236 --> 00:19:59.364
especially in our building, nobody
is making a big deal out of it,

00:19:59.448 --> 00:20:01.241
just like a lotta shit
we did in our building.

00:20:01.325 --> 00:20:03.619
We didn't give a shit
if Klay missed practice, right?
- [Green laughing]
It don't matter.

00:20:06.496 --> 00:20:08.665
- Who c—as long as you're there for the
game, as long as you, you know, you

00:20:08.665 --> 00:20:11.668
have, you healthy enough to play, like,
we didn't give a shit. Like, when you

00:20:12.544 --> 00:20:13.462
and Coach cursed each other out.
- Yeah.
[Laughing]

00:20:13.503 --> 00:20:16.006
- And literally soon as the practice
is over with, it was cool.
- Mmhmm.

00:20:16.173 --> 00:20:19.259
- Like, you know, so it was, like,
everybody was mature enough to understand,

00:20:19.259 --> 00:20:24.223
like, we come to work, we handle
our business and you be who you are.

00:20:24.223 --> 00:20:25.849
- Family. You have no kids.

00:20:25.933 --> 00:20:26.767
You're now 32.

00:20:27.559 --> 00:20:28.143
- I'll be 33.

00:20:28.268 --> 00:20:29.519
- I got three kids.

00:20:29.770 --> 00:20:30.437
I'm 31.

00:20:30.437 --> 00:20:35.317
So I, you know, I took a little
different route.
- Yeah, you OG now, man.
- But you have no kids.

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:39.279
Why? Do you want kids ultimately?
Do you not want kids?

00:20:39.404 --> 00:20:39.488
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
423
00:20:39,920 --&gt; 00:20:44,270
- I mean, that's a, that's a big commitment,
for one. And I always felt like I

00:20:43.909 --> 00:20:47.955
was just really zoned in on my work
and my alone time and my free time.

00:20:48.747 --> 00:20:51.875
Um, too much for me to, like,
lock in on something like that,

00:20:51.959 --> 00:20:55.712
you know. Eventually I do want that,
but the older I got, that gets it

00:20:55.712 --> 00:20:58.924
better, because I mature more
and more, myself more, understanding

00:20:58.924 --> 00:21:00.217
my situation a little bit more.

00:21:00.217 --> 00:21:00.968
So if I were to invite someone in

00:21:01.677 --> 00:21:04.846
or combine my life
with another person, you know, it'd

00:21:04.846 --> 00:21:06.682
be perfectly, perfect at this time.

00:21:06.682 --> 00:21:09.309
As opposed to me 10 years ago,
I wouldn't know what to do,

00:21:09.309 --> 00:21:13.522
so.
- Mmhmm.
- I think I'm, as long as I
wait, you know, uh, it's only

00:21:13.522 --> 00:21:14.356
gonna be for the better.

00:21:14.898 --> 00:21:19.820
- Do you ever worry that the
longer you wait, your kid won't

00:21:19.820 --> 00:21:21.280
understand who Kevin Durant is?

00:21:21.613 --> 00:21:25.284
- I'm glad he won't understand.
- Why is that?
- Cuz I don't want him to have to feel like

00:21:25.909 --> 00:21:30.580
he's pressured in this bubble to do what
I did, you know? And as long as I'm

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:34.876
playing, like, this bubble is always
gonna be about making it to the NBA.

00:21:34.876 --> 00:21:37.754
So if you see a little KD out here,
it's nothin but you expectin'

00:21:37.754 --> 00:21:40.090
him to be a basketball player.

00:21:40.090 --> 00:21:44.428
So, like, I don't know if my kid is even
gonna be that tall or fall into the game

00:21:44.428 --> 00:21:45.345
like I fell into it.

00:21:45.345 --> 00:21:45.846
Who knows?

00:21:45.846 --> 00:21:49.725
So I'd rather just, me tell him,
you know, over time, what I did.

00:21:50.309 --> 00:21:53.603
I don't want any pressure for anybody
just coming into my world to do what I

00:21:53.603 --> 00:21:55.939
like to do. I want 'em to explore things on their own.

00:21:56.940 --> 00:21:57.858
- So what's next for you?

00:21:57.858 --> 00:22:02.154
You got, um, you know, probably
10 more years left of hoopin.
- [Laughing]
I hope so.

00:22:02.195 --> 00:22:04.281
- What comes after that?

00:22:04.281 --> 00:22:05.282
Have you gotten there yet, or

00:22:05.282 --> 00:22:07.492
are you still just so
locked in on basketball that

00:22:07.576 --> 00:22:10.704
it is just that?
- You know, I'll definitely wanna stay
involved in the game.

00:22:11.330 --> 00:22:14.791
Um, I'm learning so much now,
I don't know where I could use

00:22:14.791 --> 00:22:17.336
it at. Coaching, GM, ownership.

00:22:18.086 --> 00:22:20.213
I feel like I'm gathering so
much knowledge that I could be

00:22:20.213 --> 00:22:21.715
useful in any part of this game.

00:22:21.882 --> 00:22:27.471
But outside of that, I've other
interests in tech world, media space,

00:22:27.721 --> 00:22:31.391
art, all of that stuff, that,
you know, that I enjoy doing in my leisure time.

00:22:31.391 --> 00:22:33.352
You know, I want to get
involved in at some point.

00:22:33.810 --> 00:22:39.524
Uh, but for now, you know what I'm about.
- [Laughing]
- You know what I enjoy to do every day.

00:22:39.524 --> 00:22:42.027
So until that time is up,
then we'll see what happens.

00:22:42.027 --> 00:22:44.488
But I feel like I'm setting up
stuff on the back end of

00:22:44.488 --> 00:22:46.073
things that I can have options.

00:22:46.698 --> 00:22:49.701
- You know, I think people look
at us, and they say: "Oh, man, you

00:22:49.701 --> 00:22:51.995
play basketball for a living.

00:22:52.079 --> 00:22:54.122
You should be happy." Which is great,

00:22:54.122 --> 00:22:54.373
right?

00:22:54.373 --> 00:22:55.540
Like, you love basketball.

00:22:55.540 --> 00:22:56.666
I love basketball.

00:22:57.000 --> 00:23:00.337
Being able to do that and make the
type of money we make is incredible.

00:23:01.338 --> 00:23:05.842
But with that comes a lot of fucking
scrutiny, comes a lotta headaches.

00:23:05.842 --> 00:23:08.553
What is the happiest
you've been as a professional?

00:23:09.137 --> 00:23:11.765
- I don't even, I don't even
like to use the word happiness.

00:23:11.973 --> 00:23:14.643
That's just a fleetin' feeling.
It can just go so up and down.

00:23:14.643 --> 00:23:15.894
I don't wanna chase that feeling.

00:23:16.395 --> 00:23:16.937
It's just not, uh,

00:23:17.729 --> 00:23:19.231
an efficient way for me to live.

00:23:19.231 --> 00:23:26.071
I feel like just having peace and
really, uh, simply just enjoying being alive

00:23:26.071 --> 00:23:27.781
every day is the best place for me to be.

00:23:27.781 --> 00:23:29.658
You know, I don't wanna
be happy and sad.

00:23:29.658 --> 00:23:31.827
Like, I don't even wanna
have to go through that.

00:23:31.827 --> 00:23:33.412
I just wanna just kind
of float through life.

